A boundary catches a raise that leaves a function called from under it, not
only an error.raise written there. The checker resolved such a call to the
boundary's handler (ErrorInvokeAndTerminate), the interpreter caught it, and
every compiled target emitted the call bare, so the raise reached the host
uncaught -- from a click handler and from an effect's @mount alike. The call
now runs under the same catch a call's own @error gets.

The lambda is a separate failure. A raise written directly in a lambda body
crashed codegen on every target ("js has no implementation of intrinsic
error.raise"): effect analysis never walked a lambda body, so the raise kept
ErrorNone and reached the generic call path. It is resolved as a raise leaving
the lambda now. And a call through a func value dropped the @error written on
it, because it has no declaration to say it can raise; that handler is the
call's own now, on every target and in the interpreter.

fyne and gtk4 are absent because neither implements boundary
(cmd/sngl/testdata/errorboundary_unimplemented.txt). The html pages are run by
cmd/sngl/testdata/call_error_handler_runs.txt.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `(?m)^\t+Risky\(5\)\n\t+m\.after` -- the call under a boundary runs under a recover, never bare
deny out/none/html/index.html `(?m)^\s+f\(\);\n\s+state\.after` -- the lambda call runs in a try, never bare

-- boundary_catches_called_raise.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import . "sngl:test"

func risky(n int) int {
    if n > 1 {
        error.raise("too big", "range")
    }
    return n * 10
}

component main node {
    var caught = ""
    var after = ""
    boundary(@error(e) { caught = caught + e.message + ";" }) {
        effect(@mount { risky(3) })
        button #stmt(text="Stmt", @click {
            risky(5)
            after = after + "s"
        })
    }
    button #lam(text="Lambda", @click {
        var f = func() { error.raise("lam", "") }
        f(@error(e) { caught = caught + "lam:" + e.message + ";" })
        after = after + "l"
    })
    text(value="{caught}|{after}")
}

func testMountRaiseIsCaught(t Test, c main) {
    t.assert(c.caught == "too big;")
}

func testHandlerCallIsCaught(t Test, c main) {
    c.stmt.click()
    t.assert(c.caught == "too big;too big;")
    t.assert(c.after == "s")
}

func testLambdaCallCatchesItsOwn(t Test, c main) {
    c.lam.click()
    t.assert(c.caught == "too big;lam:lam;")
    t.assert(c.after == "l")
}

window {
    main
}

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}
